codex
The native probe found the precise break: the inherited launch capability is present and readable, but the wheel’s Windows venv launcher creates a second Python process. The manager records PID 13192; the executing worker sees the venv redirector PID 2780 as its parent and rejects itself before hidden dispatch, so the CLI falls through to argparse and the manager later gets `BrokenPipeError`. The preserved worktree already contains the defensible direction—launch the identity-bound base interpreter on Windows—so I’m checking whether the producer is still updating that candidate before I validate or prescribe the regression.
