+### 2026-07-30 — Fixed go-v1 cycle-5 native Windows worker diagnosis and closure
+- TESTER: `TASK-260720-2g21eg` on preserved base/worktree commit `15860e3f309888845b9271a257fb95f7c2825b56`; no CocoaSkills product source or repository test file was edited by the tester.
+- LAUNCH ANCESTRY: the inherited 88-byte launch capability reached the child, but the Windows venv `python.exe` redirector made the executing interpreter a grandchild. Launching the already identity-bound base executable restored exact manager-parent/worker ancestry while retaining the fixed installed `csk.exe`, isolation flags, environment, and hidden mode.
+- LAUNCHER IDENTITY: distlib removes `.exe` from `sys.argv[0]` before `csk.cli.main`; fixed Windows-only suffix restoration recovers the bound launcher without consulting `PATH`, environment, package input, or user options.
+- IMPORT TCB: base CPython necessarily places `python_home` on `sys.path`. Admitting it without binding it would allow root-level code before worker proof, so the complete bounded Windows Python-home import tree is now identity-bound while disabled site-package directories remain excluded. Tester regressions first failed 2/2 (exit 1) on stale manager/worker root validation and omitted fixed `python314.zip`, then passed 2/2 (exit 0) after exact-root deserialization and fixed-slot archive binding.
